WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.700
The Progress tab shows every student and every unit you've assigned, with their level.

00:07.150 --> 00:15.091
Each cell shows the level, the percent right on the first try, and how many questions the student has answered.

00:15.541 --> 00:21.346
Use Sort by to put the students who need help, or the most active students,

00:21.346 --> 00:21.810
first.

00:22.260 --> 00:29.890
Print a class summary, or download everything as a spreadsheet. It always says it reflects practice,

00:29.890 --> 00:33.476
not a report-card mark. You decide proficiency.

00:33.926 --> 00:41.451
Below the table, What to look at next names the units worth a quick reteach and the students to check in with,

00:41.451 --> 00:45.419
and why. You can assign extra practice to them in one tap.

00:45.869 --> 00:54.049
You can also set a weekly question goal for the whole class. Students see one shared bar with counts only:

00:54.049 --> 00:55.900
no names and no ranking.
